Verified independently:
- **Vendor.** `libs/LibKa0s` and `tests/_kit` match `git archive v1.81.0` (56ebc24) exactly, apart from the icon prune. 19 icon files are kept, and the declaration did not change.
- **Gate at HEAD f76ba95.** `ka0s-bounded lua tests/run.lua` gave 1834 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped, exit 0. `ka0s-bounded luacheck .` gave 0 warnings / 0 errors in 151 files. The largest authored file is 1459 lines, under the 1500-line cap.
- **Commit subjects** start with LH-RV / LH-01 / LH-02, and the trailers are present.
- **Inventory.** Every workaround it lists checks out: it was either never present (no HUD, no stockDefault, no ResetToSkin, no __DrawsKey, no hand-rolled Scope guard, no close-button tint handling) or is a version or test re-pin. Nothing was removed that v1.81.0 does not cover.
- **R-1 (Ignore fonts).** The addon has no HUD. Every panel string now goes through S.Text with `{ panel = true }`, which honours Ignore fonts through P.font.
- **D-01 to D-03.** The AH drag list stays panel-scoped by default; the seam passes no `panel`. The AH table's own paints are gated on the public `Skin:GetIgnore` through NS.SkinPanelIgnored and NS.SkinPanelColor, on both the live and degraded paths. The windows are untouched.
- **Repaint order.** SetIgnore repaints the recorded S.Text calls first and then fires OnLooksChanged, so repaintAuctionTable's color writes land last.
- **NS.SkinPanelColor.** Every Ka0s Default token it reads (text.*, sem.status*, icon.hot/dim, gtip.title/value) is a literal color table in SkinDefs, so no nil reaches SetTextColor.
- **Ka0s Default** keeps the Ka0s look: no stock-look caller exists.
- **ResetToSkin opt-in rule.** Not applicable; the addon never calls ResetToSkin.
- **Mutation check.** I put master's `settings/Panel.lua` back over HEAD in a scratch copy. The new test "skin AH table: Ignore settings panel gives the table its pre-skin look, live" goes red, so it genuinely pins the change.
- **R-8 and R-11 tests.** The quality-color tests now pin a335ee exactly, and the picker test pins "Choose a skin" plus `frame.ownerLabel` = NS.BRAND, as the library's v1.81.0 changes require.
- **Golden file.** The tests/analytics_golden.txt diff is color-only: masking the `ct=` and fs color values makes both sides identical.
- **Smoke checks.** None is marked passed, and no Result line was filled in. SKIN-17's "white" tooltip line is accurate, because gtip.value is set only by Ka0s Default (WHITE) and every skin inherits it.
